**Which days of the week and hours have the highest purchase activity?**

* **Weekday**: Monday is the busiest day (16,196 orders); activity declines through the week, with Saturday the slowest (10,887). Average ticket is fairly stable (R$ 155.90–162.75), so the difference is volume, not basket size.

| Weekday | Orders | Weekday | Orders |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Monday | 16,196 | Friday | 14,122 |
| Tuesday | 15,963 | Sunday | 11,960 |
| Wednesday | 15,552 | Saturday | 10,887 |
| Thursday | 14,761 | | |

* **Hour**: purchases peak in the afternoon — 16h (6,675), 11h (6,578), 14h (6,569) — with a broad plateau from 10h to 21h and a sharp drop between 2h and 5h (188–510 orders).

**What percentage of orders are canceled or unavailable?**

1.24% of all orders (1,234 of 99,441): 625 canceled (0.63%) + 609 unavailable (0.61%).

## Customer Insights

**How many customers have made repeat purchases?**

2,997 of 96,096 unique customers (3.12%) — Olist is largely a one-time-purchase marketplace.

**How much does each customer spend on average?**

R$ 163.79 lifetime per customer; R$ 158.28 per order on average.

**Which states and cities account for the largest share of customers?**

* **States**: SP dominates with 41.94% (40,302), followed by RJ 12.88% and MG 11.71% — the Southeast concentrates ~66%.

